{"text": "State of Nowth Caroltna evitinin comer osiisies\n\nNovember 14, 2018\n\nHon. N. Lorrin Freeman\n\u2018Wake County District Attorney\nP.O. Box 31\nRaleigh, NC 27602\n\nRE: Granville County Sheriff's Office\nDear Ms. Freeman:\n\nunderstand that you have been contacted by the North Carolina State Bureau of Investigation\n(S81), about a recording that | provided to them. | would like your assistance in assessing the recording,\nand determining whether the $81 should open an investigation Into this matter.\n\nBy way of background information, | was provided this recording during my representation of\nJoshua Freeman, in August of 2014. At that time, | was still in private practice. After coming into\npossession of this recording, | contacted Special Agent John Spears at the Federal Bureau of\nInvestigation (FB!) in Cary. After speaking with him, | delivered a copy of this recording to him in August\nof 2014. 1 do not know if Special Agent Spears opened an investigation as a result of my meeting with\nhim or not.\n\nIn January of 2017, | met with Director Bob Schurmeier and Special Agent in Charge Mike\nDenning of the SBI. An Assistant Director was also in attendance, and he took possession of the\nrecording, but | understand that he left his position with the SBI shortly thereafter. On Tuesday,\nOctober 30, 2018, | provided another copy of the recording to Assistant Special Agent in Charge Lynn\nGay. | provided it after learning of an investigation in Granville County, and considered it relevant to\ntheir inquiry.\n\n| think, at this point, ! would be considered a fact witness, and it would be appropriate for you to.\nadvise the SBI about whether or not to open an investigation,\n\nSincerely,\n\nMMZS\n\nMichael D. Waters",
